  "problemStatement": {
    "formal": "\\binom{2n}{n} \\le \\frac{4^n}{\\sqrt{\\pi n}} \\quad (n \\ge 1), \\qquad\\text{and}\\qquad \\binom{2n}{n} \\sim \\frac{4^n}{\\sqrt{\\pi n}} \\ (n \\to \\infty).",
    "plain": "The parent proof (`chebyshev-bounds-oq-06`) gives the elementary two-sided bound $\\frac{4^n}{2n+1} \\le \\binom{2n}{n} \\le 4^n$. This open question asks to sharpen the **upper** bound to the Stirling-quality constant $\\frac{4^n}{\\sqrt{\\pi n}}$, and to establish the matching asymptotic $\\binom{2n}{n} \\sim \\frac{4^n}{\\sqrt{\\pi n}}$, using Stirling's approximation as available in Mathlib.",
